# TypeScript-lane test exclusions. Each line names the exact reason and says
# whether it is a permanent profile non-goal, a harness limitation, or a
# temporary implementation/compiler gap. Ordinary filesystem behavior is never
# silently reclassified as a non-goal merely because it is incomplete.
test-blob-file-backed.js: temporary cross-module implementation gap; the public fs.openAsBlob API and node:buffer file-backed Blob are not implemented yet, including immutable-stat verification, slicing, repeated reads, and web-stream delivery; this supported Node surface must return to the applicable suite when those typed runtime pieces exist
test-fs-read-empty-buffer.js: promise case requires FileHandle[Symbol.asyncDispose] through `await using`, an explicit §13 runtime Symbol-operation non-goal; sync and callback cases pass focused before exclusion
test-fs-read-offset-null.js: promise cases require FileHandle[Symbol.asyncDispose] through `await using`, an explicit §13 runtime Symbol-operation non-goal; both callback offset-null cases pass focused before exclusion
test-fs-read-promises-optional-params.js: requires util.promisify(fs.read) custom result names stored as observable Symbol metadata on the exported function, an explicit §13 non-goal
test-fs-write-file-flush.js: its sync/callback blocks replace mutable CommonJS fs.fsync/fsyncSync exports with node:test spies and require writeFile internals to observe those replacements; NTS module references are statically bound, while the applicable promise validation and success cases are covered by local/write-file-flush-static.js
test-fs-append-file-flush.js: its sync/callback blocks replace mutable CommonJS fs.fsync/fsyncSync exports with node:test spies and require appendFile internals to observe those replacements; NTS module references are statically bound, while the applicable promise validation and success cases are covered by local/write-file-flush-static.js
test-fs-constants.js: asserts a null-prototype constants object and non-writable deprecated export accessors, which require §13 prototype inspection, property descriptors, and mutable CommonJS export-object semantics
test-fs-writesync-crash.js: installs an accessor on Object.prototype with Object.defineProperty and depends on prototype-chain lookup during native error shaping, explicit §13 metaobject non-goals
test-fs-access.js: ordinary access, validation, Buffer-path, callback, and promise behavior runs through its final error assertions; completion then requires exact Error-constructor identity and engine-formatted async stack frames, §13 prototype/function-object and engine-stack non-goals
test-fs-readv-promisify.js: requires util.promisify(fs.readv) custom result names stored as observable Symbol metadata on the exported function, an explicit §13 runtime Symbol/function-object non-goal
test-fs-promisified.js: util.promisify(fs.read/fs.write/fs.exists) requires Node's per-function custom-result/custom-implementation Symbol metadata; observable Symbol hooks and function-object properties are explicit §13 non-goals
test-fs-opendir.js: calls `dir.constructor.prototype.path` and requires observable constructor/prototype function-object traversal, an explicit §13 non-goal; the applicable sync, callback, promise, async-iteration cleanup, validation, concurrency, and close cases remain covered by local/opendir-core-static.js
test-fs-promises-file-handle-close.js: requires a FileHandle native-resource finalizer to close an unreachable descriptor and emit two GC-time warnings; NTS has deterministic typed ownership but no user-defined or observable object finalizers
test-fs-promises-file-handle-dispose.js: requires FileHandle[Symbol.asyncDispose], Dir[Symbol.asyncDispose], Dir[Symbol.dispose], and `using` dispatch through those runtime Symbol hooks, explicit §13 non-goals
test-fs-promises-file-handle-read-worker.js: transfers a FileHandle host resource through Worker structured clone and transferList; shared agents and transferable host-object identity are outside the current runtime model
test-fs-write-sigxfsz.js: performs the write only in a separately spawned process using that process's builtin node:fs, which the in-process substitution harness cannot replace; it does not measure this implementation
test-fs-rmdir-recursive.js: mixes public recursive-rmdir behavior with direct import and assertions against Node's private `internal/fs/utils`; the applicable nested sync, callback, promise, error, and one-time-warning behavior is covered by local/rmdir-recursive-static.js and the six focused upstream recursive-rmdir files
test-fs-readfile-eof.js: imports fs/promises only inside separately spawned Node processes, which cannot inherit the in-process module substitution and therefore never call this implementation; unknown-sized delayed FIFO reads through callback and promise forms are covered directly by local/readfile-eof-static.js
test-fs-readfile-buffer-option.js: mixed private-binding fixture: its zero-size branches replace internalBinding('fs').fstat and mutate native request callbacks through Reflect; the applicable fixed-buffer, provider, encoding, validation, callback, sync, and real zero-sized /proc behavior is covered by local/readfile-buffer-option-static.js
test-fs-promises-readfile-buffer-option.js: mixed private-binding/disposal fixture: its zero-size branches replace internalBinding('fs').fstat, and its FileHandle cases require `await using` through the unsupported Symbol.asyncDispose hook; promise and explicitly closed FileHandle buffer behavior is covered by local/readfile-buffer-option-static.js
test-fs-syncwritestream.js: its subject is the private SyncWriteStream chosen for stdout/stderr in a separately spawned Node executable; the parent process touches fs only to hold and read the redirection file, so in-process fs substitution cannot measure the asserted implementation
test-fs-mkdtempDisposableSync.js: mixes the ordinary typed `{ path, remove }` contract with result[Symbol.dispose] calls, an explicit §13 runtime Symbol-operation non-goal; creation, idempotent removal, and creation-time path capture across chdir are covered by local/mkdtemp-disposable-static.js
test-fs-promises-mkdtempDisposable.js: mixes the ordinary typed `{ path, remove }` contract with result[Symbol.asyncDispose] calls, an explicit §13 runtime Symbol-operation non-goal; creation, idempotent asynchronous removal, and creation-time path capture across chdir are covered by local/mkdtemp-disposable-static.js
test-fs-promises-file-handle-writer.js: mixes the ordinary FileHandle writer and pull pipeline state machines with writer[Symbol.dispose]/writer[Symbol.asyncDispose], explicit §13 runtime Symbol-operation non-goals; pull/pullSync have their own untouched upstream fixtures, while ordinary writer I/O, position, limit, locking, abort, failure, validation, and close ownership are covered by local/filehandle-writer-static.js
test-fs-promises.js: the first rejection requires V8's exact async stack frame, and the file also asserts promises export property descriptors, Symbol.toPrimitive coercion, and borrowed FileHandle prototype-method receiver behavior, explicit §13 engine-stack, metaobject, Symbol-hook, and prototype/function-call non-goals; the ordinary promise operations are exercised by their focused upstream fs tests
test-fs-readfile-pipe.js: performs the asserted /dev/stdin read only in a separately spawned Node process using that process's builtin node:fs; direct delayed FIFO callback and promise reads are covered by local/readfile-eof-static.js
test-fs-readfile-pipe-large.js: performs the asserted large /dev/stdin read only in a separately spawned Node process using that process's builtin node:fs; a direct 999,999-byte FIFO callback read is covered by local/readfile-eof-static.js
test-fs-readfilesync-pipe-large.js: performs the asserted synchronous /dev/stdin read only in a separately spawned Node process using that process's builtin node:fs; a direct 999,999-byte FIFO synchronous read is covered by local/readfile-eof-static.js
test-fs-read-stream-err.js: injects its read failure by replacing the mutable CommonJS fs.read/fs.close exports after stream construction; NTS module references are statically bound, while the same read-error, stop-reading, descriptor-close, and event behavior is covered through the supported options.fs contract by local/file-stream-static.js
test-fs-read-stream-patch-open.js: after exercising the deprecated warning-only open() method, requires replacing ReadStream.prototype.open and having construction discover that runtime prototype mutation; prototype mutation and lookup are explicit §13 non-goals, while the ordinary DEP0135 method is covered by local/file-stream-static.js
test-fs-stream-construct-compat-error-read.js: builds an ersatz subclass with Object.setPrototypeOf, calls the ReadStream class as a function on an arbitrary receiver, and replaces its prototype open method; runtime prototype mutation and function-style class construction are explicit §13 metaobject/function-object non-goals
test-fs-stream-construct-compat-error-write.js: builds an ersatz subclass with Object.setPrototypeOf, calls the WriteStream class as a function on an arbitrary receiver, and replaces its prototype open method; runtime prototype mutation and function-style class construction are explicit §13 metaobject/function-object non-goals
test-fs-stream-construct-compat-graceful-fs.js: both graceful-fs compatibility subjects synthesize inheritance with Object.setPrototypeOf, invoke stream classes on arbitrary receivers, and replace prototype open methods; those runtime prototype and constructor-call mechanics are explicit §13 non-goals
test-fs-stream-construct-compat-old-node.js: both legacy compatibility subjects synthesize inheritance with Object.setPrototypeOf, invoke stream classes on arbitrary receivers, and replace prototype open methods; those runtime prototype and constructor-call mechanics are explicit §13 non-goals
test-fs-write-stream-autoclose-option.js: its final assertion inspects the autoClose accessor through WriteStream.prototype and requires an invalid-receiver property descriptor; descriptor retention/reuse, autoClose false/true, close state, and resulting bytes are covered by local/file-stream-static.js
test-fs-write-stream-change-open.js: specifically replaces mutable CommonJS fs.open/fs.close exports after construction and asserts that queued stream work observes those replacements; NTS module references are statically bound and do not perform mutable export-object lookup
test-fs-write-stream-err.js: injects its write failure by replacing mutable CommonJS fs.write/fs.close exports; NTS module references are statically bound, while two-stage write failure, callback error identity, descriptor close, and error event behavior are covered through options.fs by local/file-stream-static.js
test-fs-write-stream-flush.js: uses node:test mock.method to replace the mutable CommonJS fs.fsync export and inspect its call record; validation, true/false/null flush behavior, one actual fsync, bytes on disk, and FileHandle flushing are covered without namespace mutation by local/file-stream-static.js
test-fs-write-stream-patch-open.js: performs its subject only in a separately spawned Node process using that process's builtin node:fs, then replaces WriteStream.prototype.open; the child cannot measure this implementation and runtime prototype mutation is an explicit §13 non-goal, while ordinary DEP0135 open() behavior is covered by local/file-stream-static.js
test-fs-write-stream.js: its first block requires replacing mutable CommonJS fs.close; the remaining no-spurious-drain and invalid-chunk behavior, plus ordinary close ownership, are covered without namespace mutation by local/file-stream-static.js
